# zzz-boot-progress.patch places a stage marker inside the XNU_SHENG_PMGR block
# that sheng-platform-power.patch adds to bsd_init.c. Git applies hunks by
# context, so that block must exist first; the patch guards itself with
# #if XNU_SHENG_PMGR and is inert on boards that leave the flag off.
arch:../../../patches/xnu/sheng-platform-power.patch
arch:../../../patches/xnu/zzz-boot-progress.patch
# offline-userspace-ladder.patch adds its band 5 marker to the same opening lines of
# load_init_program() that zzz-boot-progress.patch above already touches, so it must come after
# it. It also edits load_init_program_at_path() and bsd_ast(), which no earlier patch touches.
arch:../../../patches/xnu/offline-userspace-ladder.patch
# offline-exec-count.patch touches the success branch of __mac_execve, which no earlier patch
# edits. It counts userspace execs for bands 10 to 13.
arch:../../../patches/xnu/offline-exec-count.patch
# offline-exit-hook.patch reports process exits on the panel. panic_on_crash_disabled=1 means a
# dead daemon leaves no other trace, and a 2026-10-26 measurement found processes being created
# and then vanishing. It edits proc_exit in kern_exit.c, which no earlier patch touches.
arch:../../../patches/xnu/offline-exit-hook.patch
# offline-mkdir-enospc-path.patch prints the path when mkdir reports no space. Measured
# 2026-10-27: cryptexd aborted with "mkdirat: [28: No space left on device]" while the Data
# volume still reported 31 MiB free, so the error names a different mount than the one the
# name suggests. It edits mkdir1at's out label in vfs_syscalls.c, which no earlier patch touches.
arch:../../../patches/xnu/offline-mkdir-enospc-path.patch
# The USB debug console tees printf, IOLog, kprintf and the panic drain onto a CDC-ACM port.
# It must come after zzz-boot-progress.patch above: that patch hands PE_kputc to
# boot_progress_putc and returns, so the USB init has to run before that branch or the port
# would silently capture nothing. The port's own test model checks every console byte reaches
# USB exactly once in all three PE_kputc states.
